 "schema": 4,
 "question": "B. Is this measure already running in Kymenlaakso wellbeing services county (or in the HUS university hospital area that treats its patients)?\nA. Does recent evidence support the size of effect we assume: does this measure raise the share of lung cancer patients who get curative-intent treatment, and by how much?\nMeasure: Thoracic surgeon reviews every decision not to operate. A thoracic surgeon from the university hospital sits in the county lung meeting every week and gives a second opinion before a stage I-II patient is refused surgery. Counties without their own thoracic surgeon decide about surgery without one today.",
 "area_id": "10",
 "verdict": "mixed",
 "effect_check": "weaker",
 "effect_summary_en": "",
 "supported_en": "Lau et al. 2013 (J Thorac Oncol, England) found that resection rates were 20.0% in hospitals with resident surgeons vs 11.6% in peripheral hospitals, and that rates improved most where specialist thoracic surgeons were added.",
 "not_supported_en": "The abstract read does not show the assumed 2.4-point gain from surgeon attendance at MDT meetings, and the evidence does not show a cause-and-effect link.",
