 "summary_en": "Kymenlaakso wellbeing services county says that surgery decisions and operations take place at Meilahti Hospital (HUS) in Helsinki. It also says that when surgery is not possible, treatment recommendations are made in the county's own multidisciplinary lung meeting. No county or HUS page says that a thoracic surgeon attends that meeting or reviews refusals of surgery. For the effect, the English audit study (Lau et al. 2013) found that resection rates rose most in units that added specialist thoracic surgeons. The abstract does not report the surgeon-attendance figures, and the evidence is observational.",
 "unanswered_en": "No public page was found on who attends the Kymenlaakso lung meeting, or on whether a HUS surgeon reviews patients judged not fit for surgery.",
